diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..0e3d390 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,33 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## SMS verification for sign-up
+
+Set the runtime environment variables in `.env.example`: `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`,
+`TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, an SMS-capable `TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER`, and `SMS_OTP_HOST`.
+The hostname must exactly match the public sign-up page (for example,
+`astro-news-pytrpecapa-uc.a.run.app`), without a scheme, port, or path. Production
+requires HTTPS for WebOTP. Credentials stay on the server; no texts are simulated
+when configuration is missing. The integration uses the
+[Twilio Messages API](https://www.twilio.com/docs/messaging/api/message-resource).
+
+Sign-up sends a six-digit code with an origin-bound final line (`@hostname #code`).
+WebOTP automatically extracts and submits the code where supported; native SMS
+autofill and a single accessible manual-entry field remain available. Codes expire
+after five minutes, allow five attempts, and are replaced on resend. Sending has a
+60-second cooldown. A valid code is consumed before registration; if registration
+fails, edit the account details if needed and request a new code.
+
+Challenges live in Astro's server-side session storage. Use shared session storage
+and shared rate limiting when running multiple server instances: the extra
+per-number throttle and in-flight request guard are local to each Node process.
+This application's `/api/signup` route enforces verification before forwarding to
+the existing external registration API. That external service is outside this
+repository; it must also restrict direct registration to enforce verification
+across all clients, and must support storing the forwarded `phone` field if needed.
+
+Run `node --test tests/signup.test.ts` for the isolated verification-policy tests.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
